   "id": "2099295089252012513",
   "url": "https://x.com/HEALTHCOSTtruth/status/2099295089252012513",
   "conversationId": "2099295089252012513",
   "text": "I’ve spent the last 3 days buried in the claims and contracts of a very small employer health plan.\n\nAfter almost 30 years in this industry, I thought I had seen just about everything.\n\nI was wrong.\n\nI’ve audited only a handful of claims and part of the pharmacy spend so far, and what I’ve found represents roughly a third of this group’s total claims spend.\n\nHospital claims that appear to have been materially overpaid.\n\nPharmacy costs and fees that deserve some very hard questions.\n\nTens of thousands of dollars flowing to vendors while the employer is paying a broker roughly $50,000 a year to supposedly help manage the plan.\n\nAnd the employer?\n\nThey’re just a small business trying to take care of their employees and stay in business.\n\nThey had no reason to know how to detect any of this. They hired “experts” because they run a business — not a health plan.\n\nYet somehow the employer is the fiduciary.\n\nThe people getting paid way more than they should to advise them largely are not.\n\nThat should bother every employer in America.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-14T00:32:06.000Z",
   "type": "tweet",
   "author": {
    "id": "2036770365205016576",
    "username": "HEALTHCOSTtruth",
    "name": "Christine Price",
    "url": "https://x.com/HEALTHCOSTtruth",
    "avatarUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2082536526307553280/Lr-GKcUD_normal.jpg",
