   "conversationId": "2098436766793384398",
   "text": "Proposed healthcare increase this year: 8.7%.\nHappy about that?\nPlanning to do anything different?\nI posted this before, but I redid it using a static employee count so nobody can blame enrollment changes.\nHere’s the receipt:\n\nA well-managed plan had total costs in 2025 nearly 20% LOWER than in 2017.\n\nThe traditional model?\nThe one brokers keep telling employers is “just the way it is”?\n\nThat model cost nearly 43% MORE in 2025 than in 2017.\n\nAnd while employers were paying more, employees got less:\nTraditional model deductible: up more than 25%\n\nOur client deductible: stayed at $500\n\nAnd our client never hit maximum plan spend, so the actual savings are even better than shown here.\n\nPrint it.\nPut it in front of your broker.\nAsk:\nWHY are costs up 43% with higher deductibles?\n\nSide Note:  If you still believe PPO \"discounts\" are really discounts, I'll sell you anything I own for a 75% discount from whatever charge I pull out of thin air.   That's how hospitals and networks do it.\n\n#HealthPlanCosts #EmployerHealthcare #SelfFunded #HealthcareTransparency #ERISA #FiduciaryDuty #HealthBenefits",
   "lang": "en",
