   "url": "https://x.com/HEALTHCOSTtruth/status/2097739325727285698",
   "conversationId": "2097739325727285698",
   "text": "What happens when you get rid of brokers, PPO networks, percentage-of-savings fees and all the other nonsense — and actually PAY ATTENTION to the health plan?\n\nTHIS HAPPENS.\n\nNine years of real data.\n\nUsing KFF national averages for each year as the benchmark, this employer’s actual health plan costs came in $3.89 MILLION below the national-average benchmark over nine years.  That's for a group of less than 80 employees.  Do the math.\n\nNot projected savings.\nNot modeled savings.\nNot “discounts” off inflated hospital charges.\nActual costs.\nI have the receipts:\n\n• Actual stop-loss contracts\n• Actual claims reports\n• Actual administration fees\n• Actual enrollment\n• Actual plan expenses\n\nYour renewal is coming.\n\nAsk your broker to show you what your plan has actually cost over the last nine years — and then ask them to benchmark it.  Ask them for stop loss premiums, admin fees and claims data. \n\nAnd while you’re at it, ask them whether self-funding works for employers with fewer than 100 employees.\nMost will tell you it doesn’t.\n\nEvery group I manage has fewer than 100 employees.\nThe slide below is what one of them looks like.\n\nNo smoke. No mirrors. No made-up “savings.”\n\nJust receipts.\n\nIYKYK and you desperately need to know.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-09T17:30:04.000Z",
