   "text": "Interesting conversation today.  A small city government called and asked if I'd quote them again.  \n\nMe:  Only if you guarantee that you'll try to understand how health insurance works and that self-funding carries no more risk than being fully insured.  We went down this road 3 years ago and you didn't want it bad enough.  I can't want it for you.\n\nHer:  But my broker said \"we can't wrap a self-funded plan around DPC\".\n\nMe:  Those words \"My broker said\".. is what ended our last meeting but I'll make you a deal.  Call \"your broker\" and tell him that if he will come to your office and present his quote at the same time I present mine, WITH the local news on-site with video, I'll quote it\".  \n\nHer:  He's not going to do that.\n\nMe:  Why not?  \n\nHer:  He just won't.\n\nMe:  OK - but I don't have enough hours in my day to run a quote that \"your broker\" isn't going to agree with and I will NOT place any business through him so he can continue to charge outrageous prices for doing nothing.\n\nHer:  What do I do?\n\nMe:  If you want it bad enough, give us the BOR.\n\nHer:  He'll get mad.\n\nMe:  OK - keep doing what you've been doing.  It was great talking to you.\n\nFYI, the last time I quoted this case 3 years ago, the quote was $800K less than what the broker presented with BCBS fully insured.  She made the adult decision to stay with that broker.  Today, I made the adult decision to not waste my time.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-09T01:07:26.000Z",
